ff 48%,#ffdce4 52%,#ff3b5c 75%,#8c0a28 100%)"></span><span>R +40</span><span style="margin-left:auto">Colors scale to margin, hover for the simulated vote</span></div></div></div><div class="card"><div class="stat"><div class="k">Model margin</div><div class="v r">Marshall<!-- --> +<!-- -->1.0</div></div><div class="stat"><div class="k">Simulated statewide vote</div><div><div class="cand"><i style="background:var(--dem)"></i><span>Adam Hamilton</span><span class="p">48.2<!-- -->%</span></div><div class="cand"><i style="background:var(--gop)"></i><span>Roger Marshall</span><span class="p">49.2<!-- -->%</span></div><div class="cand"><i style="background:#6f6883"></i><span>David Graham</span><span class="p">2.6<!-- -->%</span></div></div></div><div class="stat"><div class="k">Public polling average</div><div class="v" style="font-size:22px">Marshall +0.5</div><div style="font-size:12px;color:var(--mute)">Election Day polling average, LOWESS where a race has 8 or more polls</div></div><div class="stat"><div class="k">Biggest <!-- -->counties</div><div style="display:grid;gap:4px"><div class="cand"><i style="background:rgb(88,108,182)"></i><span>Johnson</span><span class="p" style="color:var(--dem2)">D +25.4</span></div><div class="cand"><i style="background:rgb(245,201,211)"></i><span>Sedgwick</span><span class="p" style="color:var(--gop2)">R +3.6</span></div><div class="cand"><i style="background:rgb(142,159,213)"></i><span>Shawnee</span><span class="p" style="color:var(--dem2)">D +14.5</span></div><div class="cand"><i style="background:rgb(16,40,140)"></i><span>Douglas</span><span class="p" style="color:var(--dem2)">D +53.9</span></div><div class="cand"><i style="background:rgb(16,40,140)"></i><span>Wyandotte</span><span class="p" style="color:var(--dem2)">D +47.5</span></div></div></div><div class="stat"><a class="btn white" style="width:max-content" href="/forecast/ks/senate">Open the race page</a></div></div></div></section></div><section class="sec"><div class="sec-h"><div><div class="eye g">Polling averages</div><h2>Trends that see past the noise</h2><p>Every public poll, weighted by recency, sample, voter screen and pollster grade. Race pages add robust LOWESS trend lines at three spans and an Election Day projection.</p></div><a class="btn more" href="/polls">All averages</a></div><div class="grid2"><div class="card"><div class="card-h"><h3><a href="/polls/approval">Trump job approval</a></h3><span class="pill r">net -18.0</span><div class="seg" role="tablist" aria-label="Range"><button role="tab" aria-selected="false" class="">30d</button><button role="tab" aria-selected="false" class="">90d</button><button role="tab" aria-selected="true" class="on">2026</button></div></div><div class="card-b" style="padding:8px 12px"><svg class="chart" viewBox="0 0 600 220" role="img" aria-label="Trump job approval average over time"><g><line class="grid" x1="42" x2="584" y1="186.6530612244898" y2="186.6530612244898"></line><text x="34" y="189.6530612244898" text-anchor="end">-40</text></g><g><line class="grid" x1="42" x2="584" y1="168.28571428571428" y2="168.28571428571428"></line><text x="34" y="171.28571428571428" text-anchor="end">-35</text></g><g><line class="grid" x1="42" x2="584" y1="149.91836734693877" y2="149.91836734693877"></line><text x="34" y="152.91836734693877" text-anchor="end">-30</text></g><g><line class="grid" x1="42" x2="584" y1="131.55102040816325" y2="131.55102040816325"></line><text x="34" y="134.55102040816325" text-anchor="end">-25</text></g><g><line class="grid" x1="42" x2="584" y1="113.18367346938774" y2="113.18367346938774"></line><text x="34" y="116.18367346938774" text-anchor="end">-20</text></g><g><line class="grid" x1="42" x2="584" y1="94.81632653061224" y2="94.81632653061224"></line><text x="34" y="97.81632653061224" text-anchor="end">-15</text></g><g><line class="grid" x1="42" x2="584" y1="76.44897959183673" y2="76.44897959183673"></line><text x="34" y="79.44897959183673" text-anchor="end">-10</text></g