></div><div class="card-b"><h3>How On Point averages polls: robust LOWESS at three spans</h3><p>Every poll is one observation at its field midpoint.</p><div class="meta">Sep 28 · Methodology</div></div></a></div></section><section class="sec"><div class="band"><div><div class="eye" style="color:var(--gold)">Commission fieldwork</div><h2 style="margin-top:8px">Statewide, district or national polling with full crosstabs.</h2><p>On Point Polling runs dual panel surveys weighted with the DSMeridian likely voter model. Campaigns, PACs and newsrooms get a topline in days, not weeks.</p></div><div style="display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:flex-end"><a class="btn white" href="/on-point-polling/services">Partner with On Point Polling</a><a class="btn" href="/contact">Contact the desk</a></div><svg viewBox="0 0 300 300" width="260" height="260" class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><defs><linearGradient id="opp-icon-grad" x1="41.75" y1="212.5" x2="258.23" y2="87.51" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><stop offset="0" stop-color="#064bf9"></stop><stop offset=".5" stop-color="#83449c"></stop><stop offset="1" stop-color="#f9064b"></stop></linearGradient></defs><path fill="url(#opp-icon-grad)" d="M197.82,150c0,26.36-21.44,47.8-47.82,47.8-3.92,0-7.78-.47-11.5-1.4v-24.43c3.54,1.86,7.44,2.84,11.5,2.84,13.69,0,24.83-11.14,24.83-24.81s-11.14-24.83-24.83-24.83-24.81,11.14-24.81,24.83v80.38c-8.18-2.52-15.89-6.27-23.01-11.19v-69.19c0-26.38,21.46-47.84,47.82-47.84s47.82,21.46,47.82,47.84ZM150,65.85c-46.38,0-84.13,37.75-84.13,84.15v92.42c7.01,6.4,14.75,11.97,23.01,16.61v-109.03c0-33.73,27.42-61.16,61.12-61.16s61.14,27.44,61.14,61.16-27.44,61.12-61.14,61.12c-3.9,0-7.75-.36-11.5-1.08v23.28c3.77.53,7.63.8,11.5.8,46.4,0,84.15-37.75,84.15-84.13s-37.75-84.15-84.15-84.15ZM150,25c-68.92,0-125,56.06-125,125,0,28.56,9.75,56.12,27.54,78.24v-78.24c0-53.75,43.73-97.46,97.46-97.46s97.46,43.71,97.46,97.46-43.71,97.46-97.46,97.46c-4.62,0-9.3-.34-13.92-1.02-3.07-.44-6.19-1.04-9.26-1.78-8.62-2.12-16